================================================================================
Historical from-scratch provenance (Alpha 2.0 and earlier)
================================================================================

Arcus is an **original, from-scratch** Mixture-of-Depths-and-Experts (MoDE)
foundation model. Its architecture, weights, and tokenizer choice are not derived
from any other model's weights:

  - The MoDE mechanism (Mixture-of-Depths + Mixture-of-Experts) is an independent
    implementation, built on top of the BoeNet research project (the author's own).
  - The tokenizer is OpenAI's `tiktoken` `o200k_base` encoding (used as a library;
Arcus ships no model weights from any third party).

================================================================================
Archived code (legacy/)
================================================================================

The `legacy/` directory contains an earlier, archived line of work that WRAPPED
HuggingFace's Qwen3 models (a Mixture-of-Depths router around a pretrained MoE).
That code is a Derivative Work of Qwen3 (Apache 2.0, Copyright the Qwen team /
Alibaba Cloud) and retains that attribution. It is not part of the from-scratch
Arcus foundation model and ships no Qwen weights.

